# L §8.1 "`missing(r)` and `covered(x, s)` are never holes" (tally 2.3, #247; the lead's P7, rulings item 12):
# a span whose end is a window isn't known to be covered, as one whose end is a `?` isn't: `false`. Pinned
# inside the cover, `true`; outside, `false`. Before: the window's hole (`a span end`).
=== m.tally
model cov
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input a: date
input w: date
input q: date
def mw: bool
  rule base v v0 = false
  rule nope beats base v v0 = true when missing(w)
def mq: bool
  rule base v v0 = false
  rule nope beats base v v0 = true when missing(q)
version st
  cite card
  governs 2026-01-01..2026-05-01
  known 2026-05-02
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-01-05, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to shop amount 100.00 PLN)
version v0
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = 2026-02-01 "c"
  w = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-10) "c"
  q = ?"which end?" "c"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
ask c_w: covered(konto, a .. w)
ask c_q: covered(konto, a .. q)
ask c_in: covered(konto, a .. w) with w = 2026-03-05
ask c_out: covered(konto, a .. w) with w = 2026-06-05
ask c_qin: covered(konto, a .. q) with q = 2026-03-05
ask c_qout: covered(konto, a .. q) with q = 2026-06-05
=== expect
c_in: true
  pinned: w = 2026-03-05
  cut 2026-06-30
c_out: false
  pinned: w = 2026-06-05
  cut 2026-06-30
c_q: false
  cut 2026-06-30
c_qin: true
  pinned: q = 2026-03-05
  cut 2026-06-30
c_qout: false
  pinned: q = 2026-06-05
  cut 2026-06-30
c_w: false
  cut 2026-06-30
warning: WARN-UNREAD def mq is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def mw is read by nothing
